 "Calibration proves the instrument; measurement assurance proves the whole measurement process stays good between calibrations. MAPs use check standards - stable artifacts measured regularly on the same process - with control charts tracking the results; drift or sudden shifts trigger investigation before product is affected. Interlaboratory comparisons extend assurance across labs. The check standard is the canary: it experiences the same environment, operators, and procedures as real work. Control limits come from history and requirements, not from wishful thinking. MAPs turn calibration from a periodic event into continuous confidence.",
