("Advanced",
 "Monte Carlo Uncertainty Evaluation (GUM Supplement 1)",
 "When models are nonlinear or distributions non-normal, the GUM's root-sum-square approximations strain - Supplement 1 (JCGM 101) prescribes Monte Carlo: assign probability distributions to each input, sample hundreds of thousands of trials through the model, and read the output distribution directly for the mean, standard uncertainty, and coverage intervals. No linearization, no normality assumptions: the histogram IS the answer. Monte Carlo validates GUM approximations and handles cases (ratios near zero, dominant rectangular inputs) where they fail. The cost is computation - trivial today - and the need to justify input distributions honestly. When the model fights linearization, simulate.",
 ["Sample input distributions through the model; read output statistics",
  "No linearization, no normality assumptions: the histogram is the answer",
  "Validates GUM approximations; handles their failure cases",
  "Justify input distributions honestly - bad inputs produce authoritative-looking nonsense",
  "When models fight linearization, simulate"],
 "Monte Carlo capability with justified input distributions.",
 "me_gum"),

("Advanced",
 "Calibration Curve Fitting",
 "Many instruments need curves, not single corrections: least-squares fitting maps instrument readings to true values across the range, with residuals checked for structure (patterns in residuals mean the model is wrong). Linear fits serve most; polynomials serve the curved - but never overfit, and never extrapolate beyond calibrated points. The fit's uncertainty joins the budget. Good practice validates the curve with independent check points, not just the fitting data. A calibration curve is a model with a domain: inside it, trustworthy; outside it, fiction. Document the model, the range, and the residuals.",
 ["Least-squares maps readings to true values across the range",
  "Check residuals for structure: patterns mean wrong model",
  "Never overfit; never extrapolate beyond calibrated points",
  "Validate with independent check points",
  "A model with a domain: inside trustworthy, outside fiction"],
 "Curve fitting with residual analysis and independent verification.",
 "me_calcurve"),

